{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 49, :comments ["<b>my refuge from my enemies</b> — Some say: Saul and his men." "<b>even from those who rise against me</b> — They are the nations of the lands." "<b>from a man of violence</b> — The king of the Philistines, for it is far-fetched that he would say this of Saul, 'a man of violence.' It is also possible that it is an allusion to Saul, as he said: 'from the wicked comes forth wickedness' [2 Samuel 3:39]."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:27:46.587672010Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}